      "explanation": "The script makes a network request to an external API, which could pose security risks, such as potential exposure to network sniffing or man-in-the-middle attacks. The custom API endpoint, 'https://api.example.com/v1/forecast', might not be well-secured.",
      "remediation": "Ensure that the external API is properly secured and supports HTTPS. Consider adding network-level security measures, such as using a firewall or content security policies (CSP), and validate the API's security controls.",
      "code_snippet": "\n\ndef forecast(city):\n    url = \"https://api.example.com/v1/forecast\" + urllib.parse.urlencode({\"city\": city})\n    req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + os.environ[\"WEATHER_API_KEY\"]})\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=10) as resp:\n        return json.load(resp)",
